# ── CLIENT-side config (Vite) — copy to .env — everything here is PUBLIC:
# it gets baked into the JavaScript bundle on every visitor's machine.
# The delivery credentials (NOTIFY_TELEGRAM_*) live SERVER-side in .dev.vars
# (local — copy from .dev.vars.example) or Cloudflare → Settings →
# Variables & Secrets (production).
#
# Routing priority (auto-detected at build time):
#   1. own Cloudflare Pages Function → uncomment VITE_CONTACT_API below
#      (inquiries arrive as a Telegram message on your phone — the only path)
#   2. mailto fallback (automatic when the flag is absent — e.g. a GitHub
#      Pages deploy without the function)

# 1 — own Cloudflare Pages Function (Telegram delivery behind it):
# VITE_CONTACT_API=/api/contact

# 2 — mailto fallback recipient (public info; default lives in src/data/site.js):
VITE_CONTACT_EMAIL=hello@ivanbuilds.dev
